„­bible_version£KJV¤book1§chapter¨sections—…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„If there be therefore any consolation in Christ, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any bowels and mercies,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`fulfil ye my joy, that ye be likeminded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwLet nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙQLook not every man on his own things, but every man also on the things of others.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book1§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8Let this mind be in you, which was also in Christ Jesus:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKwho, being in the form of God, thought it not robbery to be equal with God:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpbut made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙuand being found in fashion as a man, he humbled himself, and became obedient unto death, even the death of the cross.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[Wherefore God also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name:¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
